  "releaseNotes": "ContentTypes gives names ending in .arw, .dng, .cr2 and .nef their camera raw types: image/x-sony-arw, image/x-adobe-dng, image/x-canon-cr2 and image/x-nikon-nef. So an upload of one without a type is stored as an image, which a ByteShelf server 3.1.0 or later makes previews of. See https://github.com/AdamTovatt/byte-shelf/blob/client-v4.0.1/ByteShelfCommon/README.md",
